The Darwin 26 MAC hook mpo_proc_check_service_port_derive (mac_policy_ops slot 44). xnu-12377 has a void notification,
mpo_proc_notify_service_port_derive, in that slot; Darwin 26 made it an access check that returns an errno.
macOS 27's EndpointSecurity fills slot 44 with es_proc_check_service_port_derive, signed with the int function type,
so xnu's void-typed call failed pointer authentication on the first connection port (mach_port_construct). As in
the Darwin 26 kernel, a denial frees the derived sandbox label and the port is not created (KERN_DENIED).
--- a/security/mac_policy.h
+++ b/security/mac_policy.h
@@ -3970,11 +3970,13 @@
 	);
 
 /**
- *  @brief Notification of connection port derivation from service port
+ *  @brief Access control check for connection port derivation from service port
  *  @param cred Subject process credential
  *  @param sp_info Service port info
  *
  *  Called when a process derives a connection port from a service port.
+ *  This is the Darwin 26 form of the hook (proc_notify_service_port_derive,
+ *  a notification, in xnu-12377); macOS 27's EndpointSecurity implements it.
  *
  *  Notes:
  *  - Port derivation is only mandatory if the receiving end of the
@@ -3982,8 +3984,11 @@
  *  - MAC policies should not perform upcalls or expensive operations in
  *    this hook.
  *  - Only called on macOS.
+ *
+ *  @return Return 0 if access is granted, otherwise an appropriate value for
+ *  errno should be returned; the connection port is then not created.
  */
-typedef void mpo_proc_notify_service_port_derive_t(
+typedef int mpo_proc_check_service_port_derive_t(
 	kauth_cred_t cred,
 	struct mach_service_port_info *sp_info
 	);
@@ -6082,7 +6087,7 @@
 	mpo_file_notify_close_t                 *mpo_file_notify_close;
 
 	mpo_proc_check_launch_constraints_t     *mpo_proc_check_launch_constraints;
-	mpo_proc_notify_service_port_derive_t   *mpo_proc_notify_service_port_derive;
+	mpo_proc_check_service_port_derive_t    *mpo_proc_check_service_port_derive;
 	mpo_proc_check_set_task_exception_port_t *mpo_proc_check_set_task_exception_port;
 	mpo_proc_check_set_thread_exception_port_t *mpo_proc_check_set_thread_exception_port;
 
